  "preamble": "Spirantization with loss of glottalization: Proto-East-Cushitic *kʼ, kept as [kʼ] in Oromo and Highland East Cushitic, appears as uvular q in Somali and as the fricative /x/ in Rendille (Heine 1978 states the correspondence R x : S q : Boni ʔ/∅). The Rendille change probably went through the Proto-Sam uvular *q, and some Rendille speakers still use [q].",
